# Git Safety

Before any commit:

1. Run `git status --short`.
2. Review `git diff --stat`.
3. Stage only intended files.
4. Review `git diff --cached --stat` and, when appropriate, `git diff --cached`.
5. Generate a scoped commit message.

Never push, force-push, reset hard, clean untracked files, delete branches, rewrite history, or tag releases without explicit approval.
